/*
Problem: Insert into a Binary Search Tree (LC 701)
Topic: Binary Search Tree / Recursion

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

Use the Binary Search Tree property.

• If the value is smaller than the
  current node, insert it into the
  left subtree.

• If the value is greater than the
  current node, insert it into the
  right subtree.

When we reach a NULL pointer,
create the new node there.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. If the current node is NULL:

   Create a new node and return it.

2. If val is smaller than root->val:

   Insert into the left subtree.

3. If val is greater than root->val:

   Insert into the right subtree.

4. Return the current root.

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

        4
       / \
      2   7
     / \
    1   3

Insert:

5

Result:

        4
       / \
      2   7
     / \  /
    1  3 5

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

        5
       /
      3
     /
    2

Insert:

4

Result:

        5
       /
      3
     / \
    2   4

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

The BST property guarantees that
every recursive call moves closer to
the correct insertion position.

The first NULL encountered is exactly
where the new node should be placed.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(h)

h = Height of the BST.

Balanced BST : O(log n)

Worst case (skewed) : O(n)

--------------------------------------------------

Space : O(h)

Recursion stack.

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

Binary Search Tree
Recursion
*/

class Solution {
public:

    TreeNode* insertIntoBST(TreeNode* root, int val) {

        // Found insertion position
        if (root == NULL) {

            return new TreeNode(val);
        }

        // Insert into right subtree
        if (val > root->val) {

            root->right =
                insertIntoBST(root->right, val);
        }

        // Insert into left subtree
        else if (val < root->val) {

            root->left =
                insertIntoBST(root->left, val);
        }

        return root;
    }
};
